  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 229 AM EDT Wed Jul 22 2026\n\nCool and almost early Fall-like temperatures are being seen across \nthe U.P. this morning as observing stations are already reporting \ntemperatures in the mid-40s. With mostly clear skies continuing \nthrough the rest of the pre-dawn hours, we could see a few spots \nbottom-out and dip into the upper to maybe even mid 30s! Otherwise, \noutside of the interior west, expect the rest of the U.P. to bottom \nout in the 40s (maybe the lower 50s over the Keweenaw). \n\nContinuing into today and the rest of the work week, expect \ngenerally calm weather and mostly sunny skies as high pressure \nridging moving through today flattens out and eventually leaves \ntowards New England for the latter half of the work week. Behind the \nridging moving through, warm air advection moves into the area. \nThus, expect a general warming trend from around to just-below \nnormal temperatures today to above well above normal temperatures by \nthis weekend.\n\nOutside of a less than 10% of rain showers/storms skirting the area \nThursday night into Friday, rain chances look to finally return on \nSaturday as a cold front drops through the area. With 1 to 3 kJ/kg \nof MUCAPE potentially available and 0-6 km bulk shear around 30 to \n40 kts, some severe weather could be seen on Saturday with the cold \nfront's passage. With another front/shortwave potentially moving \nthrough on Sunday into Monday morning and atmospheric shear and \npotential energy remaining high, additional severe weather chances \nare possible. Precipitation chances finally look to end as we head \ninto the middle of next week as high pressure ridging amplifies over \nthe central CONUS and another back door cold front moves down from \nnorthern Ontario. \n\nOne final note worth mentioning: given the strong winds over Lake \nSuperior yesterday and last night, high waves are still creating \ndangerous swimming conditions across the Lake Superior beaches east \nof Marquette County this morning into this afternoon. While the \nwaves and rip current risk will decrease, dangerous swimming \nconditions are looking to remain until the late afternoon hours \n(around 5 PM EDT) over Alger County and Luce County until sunset \nthis evening. Therefore a Beach Hazard Statement has been issued for \nAlger County until 5 PM EDT today.",
